WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:01.299
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.299 --> 00:00:05.070
Today's video is coming to you in three very
special parts: business, exciting announcements,

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.190
and mosquito-borne illnesses.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.190
Part one- business.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:11.460
So Hank, in last week's video, I asked people
if we should turn on pre-roll advertisements

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.930
for Vlogbrothers, and then, if so, what we
should do with that revenue.

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:17.410
Tens of thousands of people responded, Hank,
and they voted overwhelmingly that we should

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.409
turn on pre-rolls and that we should split
the income between the Foundation to Decrease

00:00:21.409 --> 00:00:25.329
World Suck, and a fund that will help out
educational video projects.

00:00:25.329 --> 00:00:28.789
So that's what we're going to do, and Nerdfighters,
we will keep you up to date on how that money

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:29.789
is spent.

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:30.789
By the way Hank, did you notice that I have
a tan?

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:33.840
I've been experimenting a little bit with
outside, although I can't, in good faith,

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:34.840
recommend it.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.789
Also I've got some puff because I'm in control
of my own haircut schedule for the first time

00:00:38.789 --> 00:00:39.789
in six months.

00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:43.640
People in Hollywood have lots of opinions
about how often you should get a haircut.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.940
Part two- exciting announcement.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.300
Sooo I am going to East Africa with Bill Gates.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.070
I am very excited about this trip, not only
because I get to hang out with Bill Gates,

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:56.519
but also because I get to meet a lot of people
who are doing important work in health and

00:00:56.519 --> 00:00:57.519
agriculture.

00:00:57.519 --> 00:00:59.320
And hopefully I'm going to learn a lot and
make a bunch of videos.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.879
But that brings me to part three- mosquito-borne
illnesses.

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:06.330
The light keeps changing; it's like a 2007
Vlogbrothers video.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:10.390
So Hank, as you know some of my anxiety problems
center on physical health, and when my doctor

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:14.710
was giving me the vaccines to get ready for
this trip, he said "You should read the CDC

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:19.160
web pages about the places you'll be visiting",
and that was a terrible idea.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:22.350
Because those websites are like, "malaria
mosquitoes bite mostly at night-time, while

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:26.670
yellow fever mosquitoes bite primarily during
the day, and West Nile mosquitoes bite at

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:27.670
dawn and dusk."

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:32.150
And reading that stuff made me think I am
going to a place where disease-ridden mosquitoes

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:33.720
bite in shifts.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:37.350
So I called my doctor and I was like, "This
doesn't seem safe at all", and he said, "You

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:40.770
should read the Indiana State Department of
Health webpage"!

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:44.560
So I did, and in addition to having information
about the West Nile virus, which I knew to

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.420
be worried about, there was a warning about
the Arbo virus, which I'd never even heard

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:49.420
of.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.290
And one about Chikungunya virus which I don't
even know how to pronounce.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.640
Hank, I don't want to be killed by something
that I can't pronounce!

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.940
I think my doctor thought I would emerge from
that experience less anxious, but quite the

00:01:58.940 --> 00:01:59.940
opposite.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:03.530
Anyway Hank, all of this is just to say that
I've recently become, I think, the only person

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:07.450
in the history of the world to read the entire
Indiana State Department of Health website.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:11.140
No, wait, I also had another point, which
is that we have excellent healthcare facilities

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:13.270
and information here in the United States.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:17.010
We've got great infrastructure, the power
very rarely goes off in health clinics, and

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:20.810
all that stuff helps us to deal with mosquito-borne
illnesses and other communicable diseases

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:21.810
relatively effectively.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:25.120
And I'm going to East Africa, Hank, to see
how they've dramatically improved healthcare

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.730
and reduced infant mortality in the last twenty
years.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:31.520
And also to see how much work there still
is to be done and where we can help.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.440
I'm gonna make a bunch of videos, but they
probably won't be uploaded during my trip,

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:38.970
so in the meantime I'm going to make a video
about Behind the Beautiful Forevers, the Nerdfighter

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.090
Book Club pick for summer.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.170
If you haven't read it, now's the time because
A) it will make next week's video more enjoyable,

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.170
and B)

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:45.170
it's excellent.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.760
It won the Pulitzer Prize, for God's sakes.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.280
But anyway yeah, I will schedule that video
to upload next Tuesday so that I don't get

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:51.280
punished.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.340
Speaking of punishments, Hank, you owe us
one!

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.760
Nerdfighters, I need punishment suggestions
for Hank in the comments.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.400
Hank, DFTBA, I will see you on Friday.

